Have I really forgotten...
 something important?

00:17:10.610 --> 00:17:12.800
What? What could it be?

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:13.800
Don't be naughty!

00:17:16.030 --> 00:17:18.350
If I'm not mistaken... Yes!

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:20.560
When I wrote this letter...

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:27.230
Uh, umm...

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:34.610
I don't know what I should write.

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:37.980
Kazuki-chan? What are you still doing here?

00:17:37.980 --> 00:17:40.570
Yuuji-kun and Marie-chan are leaving.

00:17:40.570 --> 00:17:43.320
Y-Yeah, I'll be right there.

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:54.590
To Yuuji

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:54.590
Don't forget, okay?

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:12.150
Don't be naughty!

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:12.150
~Kazuki

00:18:22.670 --> 00:18:24.860
Kazuki-chan, Kazuki-chan!

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:30.920
What are you doing?! We're about to leave.

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:35.670
What am I doing? 
Hey, I can do whatever I want!

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:36.550
To Yuuji

00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:38.360
I guess so...

00:18:38.740 --> 00:18:39.740
Here!

00:18:39.740 --> 00:18:40.550
What's that?

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:41.800
A pinky promise.

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:45.560
Why do I have to I make
 a pinky promise with you?

00:18:45.910 --> 00:18:49.810
So that you won't forget about us, Kazuki-chan. {So that Kazuki-chan won't forget about us.}

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:51.520
Come on, hurry up.

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:58.840
Pinky promise not to lie, 
stick a needle in your eye... {yes, I know the line is really "swallow 10,000 needles," but this rhymes :) }

00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:00.860
Promise made! {sb ok}

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:05.330
We won't forget about you,
 so you'd better not forget about us.

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:12.790
Take that!

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:16.800
Geez, what are you doing, Yuuji!?

00:19:19.160 --> 00:19:20.510
See ya!

00:19:21.820 --> 00:19:23.510
Ah, the letter!

00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:33.230
H-How could I have forgotten?!

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:38.280
But was the "old" Yuuji-kun...
 really such a good guy?

00:20:00.580 --> 00:20:02.130
Hatsune-oneesama.

00:20:02.410 --> 00:20:07.070
Say, Marie-chan, are you
 hiding anything from me?

00:20:07.910 --> 00:20:10.430
No, not at all.

00:20:11.450 --> 00:20:13.140
Oh my, is that so? {stc}

00:20:13.140 --> 00:20:13.380
Oh my, is that so? {stc}

00:20:13.380 --> 00:20:16.350
Perhaps I'm just over-thinking things?

00:20:17.430 --> 00:20:19.280
By the way, Marie-chan...

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:22.400
Do you like beetles?

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:29.730
You mustn't try to deceive me.{Ryo: You won't succeed in trying to hide it from me. // missed the "dame" part which implies more of a "shouldn't" than a "won't"}

00:20:29.730 --> 00:20:31.620
Out with it now.

00:20:32.100 --> 00:20:34.370
What might be going on?

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:37.970
Come on, come on...

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:46.410
B-But...

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:49.790
...Yuuji used to be such a nice boy.

00:20:50.870 --> 00:20:54.670
<i>...people tend to have very selective memories about their pasts.</i>

00:20:58.600 --> 00:20:59.700
I...

00:21:00.060 --> 00:21:03.860
...thought I had remembered 
everything about Yuuji...

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:08.190
Oh my, oh my.

00:21:11.020 --> 00:21:12.660
I want to know too.

00:21:14.770 --> 00:21:15.920
What did you say?!

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:20.460
Rolling dash!

00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:22.880
Hatsune-kun.

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:25.260
It's all right.

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:26.380
Stop it!

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:27.470
Thank you, Kazuki!

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:29.090
Please allow me to inspect it!

00:21:29.090 --> 00:21:30.560
Kazuki!!

00:21:32.030 --> 00:21:34.430
How about THIS?!

00:21:35.650 --> 00:21:37.400
Don't joke around!

00:21:38.380 --> 00:21:40.150
The old Yuuji...

00:21:40.840 --> 00:21:43.100
...has always been by my side.

00:21:43.600 --> 00:21:45.660
Right before my eyes...

00:21:47.040 --> 00:21:48.990
Kazuki-chan, bad news!

00:21:48.990 --> 00:21:52.240
What's wrong, Onee-chan? 
Why're you panicking?

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:55.540
Yuuji-kun and Marie-chan{Ryoumi: Yuuji-kun and the others... // what "other*s*" could she be talking about?!?!?!} are going to move away again!

00:22:06.220 --> 00:22:14.850
The first time we met was on that sunlit veranda... {fi, link}

00:22:06.220 --> 00:22:14.850
Hajimete deatta hidamari no BERANDA

00:22:14.850 --> 00:22:20.480
Do you remember that place? {video fi, fo}

00:22:14.850 --> 00:22:20.480
Oboeteru kono basho?

00:22:21.860 --> 00:22:31.700
Spending time together was like breathing air, {sc, sc}

00:22:21.860 --> 00:22:31.700
Maru de kuuki no you na futari no jikan

00:22:31.700 --> 00:22:38.500
and we didn't realize the beauty of that placid time. {fo? or sc}

00:22:31.700 --> 00:22:38.500
SUTEKI na koto kizukanai PLACID TIME

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:46.010
Our feelings of missing each other gave birth to... {sc, link}

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:46.010
Aitai kimochi kara umareta

00:22:46.010 --> 00:22:50.640
...the dreams that bloomed in our hearts, {link, link}

00:22:46.010 --> 00:22:50.640
Kokoro ni saku yume wo

00:22:50.640 --> 00:22:56.270
which became more and more colorful. {link, link}

00:22:50.640 --> 00:22:56.270
Nan domo irozuiteku dakara

00:22:56.270 --> 00:23:03.480
Will you let me stay by your side? {link, link}

00:22:56.270 --> 00:23:03.480
Anata no tonari ni isasete ne

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:07.860
I hope our silhouettes... {link, link}

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:07.860
Futatsu no SHIRUETTO

00:23:07.860 --> 00:23:19.750
...will continue this endless story tomorrow. {link, fo}

00:23:07.860 --> 00:23:19.750
Ashita mo tsuzuku to ii na endless story

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:27.460
Next Episode

00:23:26.370 --> 00:23:29.970
Even now, Yuuji has a lot of good points.

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:34.970
Maybe I've been trying to
 force my own ideals onto him.

00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:39.970
The Veranda and
 the Paper Airplane

00:23:35.320 --> 00:23:39.490
The next episode is the last one: 
The Veranda and the Paper Airplane.
